EXT. WHALE-RIB BRIDGE - DAWN

A colossal skeleton arches over a fogbound chasm. Ribs the width of oaks form a walkway. Prayer flags snap from the vertebrae.

SERAPHINA OKONKWO-DREY (30s, hooded cloak, staff of white wood) steps onto the bridge. BRAM THE LAME (50s, iron crutch) shuffles behind her. TASHI (12, goat bell on a cord) skips ahead. Last, GREYMOOR (ageless, antlered, silver eyes) waits on the far side.

SERAPHINA
Stay on the bones.

TASHI
Which bones?

BRAM
All of them, you fool.

The bridge shudders. A rib cracks. Seraphina grabs Tashi's collar, Bram lunges for the rail, and all three crash to their knees as a gap opens ahead.

GREYMOOR
You are late.

SERAPHINA
The tide was early.

GREYMOOR
The tide was never yours.

Greymoor raises one hand. Mist rises, thick and white. The bridge heals itself with a groan. Bram stands, stunned. Tashi laughs, a bright note.

TASHI
Again!

Seraphina and Greymoor lock eyes. Neither blinks.
